FIXME: GRIB input of multi-format.grib #12/#13, by gridSpec and by GRIB keys (legacy) differ

Why
  Both messages are regular_ll, GRIB1 (millidegree), first longitude of a grid point off the origin by a fraction of the
  increment (0.1171875 = 15/128 and 0.0703125 = 9/128, encoded as 0.117 and 0.07). ecCodes' gridSpec (GribToSpec,
  feature/eckit-geo-grids, not yet upstream) recovers the intended bounds (snapping to a fraction of the increment, within
  the angular precision); mir's GRIB keys input takes them as encoded. The regridded messages are identical, only the
  input grid (its reference) differs:
    #12  by gridSpec {"grid":[0.234375,0.15625],"order":"i+j+","reference":[0.1171875,0.078125]}
         by GRIB keys {"grid":[0.234375,0.156250217202433],"order":"i+j+","reference":[0.117,0.0781251086012163]}
    #13  by gridSpec {"grid":[0.140625,0.0937498697238145],"order":"i+j+","reference":[0.0703125,0.0468749348619072]}
         by GRIB keys {"grid":[0.140625,0.0937498697238145],"order":"i+j+","reference":[0.07,0.0468749348619072]}
  The gridSpec results are the correct ones.

What
  Once ecCodes with the GribToSpec bounds recovery is upstream (and required by mir), and legacy input agrees (or is
  retired in favour of gridSpec input), restore the checks below and delete this file.

